Hi

You’re interested in traveling the world, learning about different cultures, and developing global leadership skills and we are here to help you succeed in a global business environment!  The Bachelor of Global Management program offered through ASU’s Thunderbird School of Global Management will provide you with the experience, education, and opportunities you need to capitalize on your ability to thrive in the global marketplace. 

Take a few minutes to check out these videos to learn how Thunderbird will connect you to the world through the Bachelor of Global Management program.  Listen to videos from:

Collin Shepherd | Undergraduate Admission Specialist for Thunderbird

Dr. Roy Nelson | Academic Director

Katelyn Lynch | Current Bachelor of Global Management student

To enter our virtual space to watch videos and live chat, follow this link http://bit.ly/BGMVirtualSpace 

You will reach a login page. You will have to create a login, so click on the link to sign up. 

Have questions?  Tune in to our live chats where you can have your questions answered by us.  Whether its questions about your opportunities to travel abroad, what classes you will be taking, or campus life and activities, we will be here to answer all your questions! 

Once logged in, you will be at the Thunderbird booth where you can watch videos and download documents about the Bachelor of Global Management program. Click on the Chat Hall link at the top of the virtual space to chat with Thunderbird staff and current students. 

